                "RBAC, input validation, no shared state"
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "525912e5-800d-466a-abfc-942f30ae1e76",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 1,
      "data": {
        "title": "DFD — o mapa pra pensar ameaças"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "f22afa65-faa4-43e2-9cb4-7cce933f9ed2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "content": [
              {
                "text": " Data Flow Diagram é o template pra aplicar STRIDE. Desenhe "
              },
              {
                "text": "entidades",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (user, DB, serviço externo), "
              },
              {
                "text": "processos",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "text": "data stores",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " e "
              },
              {
                "text": "trust boundaries",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (onde nível de confiança muda). "
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "56722983-c5b5-442c-8a26-351d6e4c2015",
          "type": "code_block",
          "position": 1,
          "data": {
            "language": "text",
            "code": "[Browser]  ─HTTPS─▶  [API]  ─TLS─▶  [DB]\n           ▲                │\n           │                └─HMAC──▶ [Webhook Target]\n        trust boundary:\n        - User → API: spoofing (auth fraca?), tampering (TLS cert errado?)\n        - API → DB: info disclosure (cred hardcoded?), elevation (SQLi?)\n        - API → Webhook: tampering (replay sem HMAC?), repudiation (sem log?)"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "568580c9-fe52-4467-9498-945c918aade4",
          "type": "callout",
          "position": 2,
          "data": {
            "variant": "info",
            "title": "",
            "content": "Cada seta que cruza trust boundary é candidato a ameaça. Sente com o STRIDE ao lado e pergunte pra cada seta: que S/T/R/I/D/E pode acontecer aqui?"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a98d5d7d-3a2b-4c8f-8ca4-ff965dc2ca74",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 2,
      "data": {
        "title": "DREAD → CVSS: priorizando"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "09d488fd-b6ba-4354-8a41-87743b3ea397",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "content": [
              {
                "text": " DREAD soma pontos em Damage/Reproducibility/Exploitability/Affected/Discoverability. Foi criticado por ser subjetivo. "
              },
              {
                "text": "CVSS 4.0",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (Common Vulnerability Scoring System) substituiu em 2026 pra priorização objetiva — vetor com attack surface, complexity, privileges required, user interaction, scope, CIA impact. "
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "4499f8b7-9b6d-4e3d-b718-5a3f5ec7ae62",
          "type": "code_block",
          "position": 1,
          "data": {
            "language": "text",
            "code": "CVSS 4.0 Base Score exemplo:\nAV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H\n= 10.0 (Critical) — atacante via rede, sem auth, impacto total"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "e3ee539d-4328-4a22-aaca-826bb0ca581a",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 3,
      "data": {
        "title": "Operacionalizando: Threat Dragon ou markdown"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "6e463641-b949-42f0-9f64-6bc39346652f",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "content": [
              {
                "text": " Ferramentas: "
              },
              {
                "text": "OWASP Threat Dragon",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (open source, desenha DFD), "
              },
              {
                "text": "Microsoft Threat Modeling Tool",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (free, Windows), "
              },
              {
                "text": "PyTM",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (code-first em Python). Alternativa pragmática: markdown template no repo com DFD em mermaid + tabela STRIDE. Versiona junto com o código. "
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "3cd7e781-5449-4083-ba05-ccd1819e8eec",
          "type": "callout",
          "position": 1,
          "data": {
            "variant": "success",
            "title": "",
            "content": "Integre no PR template: \"Qual trust boundary este PR toca? Que STRIDE aplicamos?\". Faz threat modeling virar hábito, não evento."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}